From 46dd21a4825126311c5d77f81027fff54997601e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:37:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(ui): one command table for the ribbon, the menu bar
 and the keys

The new panes/table.rs holds each fixed command once: id, label, ribbon
group, menu and shortcut. The ribbon's anchor groups, a new in-app menu
bar (File, Edit, Setup, Operation, Inspect, View) and the keyboard layer
all read it. Menu rows run the existing actions layer; the menu adds no
state change. Tests check that the ribbon and the menu list the same ids,
that each command has a label, tip and enabled rule, and that no two
commands share a shortcut.

Fixes #4484

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
